w("refusal.COUNTERPARTY_NOT_OVERSIGHT", "An oversight or audit request goes to an oversight or audit body. The jurisdiction profile marks the office this action is addressed to as not one. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.COUNTERPARTY_REFUSED", "An action says who it is addressed to: an office by its official role and the body it belongs to; a reporter, an organization or another team by a role and the organization; an audience described in words; or an undetermined addressee with a few words on what is known and what would settle it. This write carried a placeholder, a bare name outside those shapes, a person, or an addressee that said two things at once, so nothing was written. Leaving the addressee out is allowed while the action is a draft.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.COURT_LINK_TARGET_NOT_LAW", "A court's reading is linked to a portion of a statute, regulation, ordinance or policy, and the standard named is none of these. Nothing was written.", note="law-relations' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CO_ATTESTATION_UNACKNOWLEDGED", "A load-bearing document has no trusted timestamp and co-archive. Retry them, or acknowledge publishing it as self-attested only, with a reason. Nothing was written.", note="case-disclosures' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.CREDENTIALS_MISSING", "This tool needs a key or sign-in detail that was not given, named beside this. Nothing was added.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DECISION_WITHOUT_OUTCOME", "A decision carries its outcome as the body gave it. If the body stated none, record none_stated so the record says so rather than leaving it blank.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DEEPER_CHECKS_UNREADABLE", "The deeper checks your team asked for could not be read just now, so none was started or asked about. They are read again on the next round.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DEEPER_CHECK_BUDGET_SPENT", "Every outside tool your team uses for deeper checks has used its allowance for this month, so no check was asked for. The allowance starts again on the first of the month.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DESCRIPTOR_MALFORMED", "The description of this tool is missing something it must state, named beside this. Nothing was added.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DETERMINATION_NOT_A_PARTICIPANT", "Only a member who has joined this project records its determinations. Join the project first. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DETERMINATION_ONLY_BY_ITS_ACT", "A determination is recorded only by the determination act, and never edited: a correction is a new determination that supersedes it. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DETERMINATION_SUPERSEDED", "That determination has been superseded, and a superseded determination is not acted on or superseded again. Use the determination that replaced it. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DETERMINATION_TOO_LARGE", "This names more than one determination or comparison may carry. Split it into several. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DETERMINATION_UNREADABLE", "No determination can be read here, so the actions available against its offices cannot be listed.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DISCLOSURE_NOT_STANDING", "One of the conflicts disclosed is not an unresolved conflict on this case's findings: it may have been resolved since. Read the list again. Nothing was published.", note="case-disclosures' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DOCUMENT_COPY_UNDETERMINED", "A document this case relies on could not be checked for the details a member's file can carry, so what the published case would show of it is not known. Try again. Nothing was written.", note="case-disclosures' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DUE_CITE_NOT_GOVERNING", "A due date names the law it comes from, and that law must be one of those a member has stated govern this action. State the governing laws first, then cite one of them exactly as listed.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DUE_HALF_STATED", "A due date is stated together with the citation it comes from, or not at all. With none stated the record reads it as undetermined, which is honest.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DUE_NOT_A_DATE", "A due date is written as a calendar date, YYYY-MM-DD.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.DUPLICATE_PATH", "The list of this case file's contents puts two documents under the same name, so one download could be read two ways. This team's Civicsmith will not hand over a case file that says two things about one name. Each document can still be asked for on its own. Nothing was changed.", note="public-read's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.EDGE_NOT_PROPOSED", "That stage is not proposed, so there is nothing to decline. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.ENVELOPE_DATES_DISAGREE", "The document being filed says when it was made or last changed, and the request that carried it says a different time. The record keeps its history in the order those dates give, and it goes by the document, so it stops and tells you both. Nothing was written. Send it again with the request giving the document's dates, or giving none, or change the document first.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.ENVELOPE_STATE_DISAGREES", "The document being filed says where it stands, and the request that carried it says something different. Where a thing stands decides who may move it and what may cite it, and the record goes by the document, so it stops and tells you both. Nothing was written. Send it again with the request saying what the document says, or saying nothing about it, or change the document first.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.ENVELOPE_TITLE_DISAGREES", "The document being filed gives itself one name, and the request that carried it gives another. The record goes by the document, and names are held unique across your team's Civicsmith, so rather than file it under a name it does not bear it stops and tells you both. Nothing was written. Send it again with the request naming the document's title, or naming none, or change the document first.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.ENVELOPE_TYPE_DISAGREES", "The document being filed says what kind of thing it is, and the request that carried it says something different. The record goes by the document, so rather than file an action as information — or the reverse — and index it as neither, it stops and tells you both answers. Nothing was written. Send it again with the request naming the type the document names, or change the document first.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.ESCALATION_CARRIES_NO_JUDGMENT", "An escalation records no significance, severity, priority, urgency, rank or score. Whether a breach warrants action, and how urgently, is the members' judgment, made with the consequences in front of them. Send the act without it. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.ESCALATION_ENDED", "This escalation has ended: compliance was restored and the consequences addressed. An ended escalation is never reopened; a new breach is a new determination. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.ESCALATION_HISTORY_REWRITTEN", "An escalation's history is never edited; each act adds to it. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.ESCALATION_NOT_A_PARTICIPANT", "An escalation is opened by a member who has joined the project that made the determination. Join the project first. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.ESCALATION_NO_REASON", "This act needs a reason, in your own words, of up to 2,000 characters. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.EXTENT_NOT_APPLICABLE", "Which part of a document a citation rests on is something a QUESTION's basis records, and the thing citing here is a case. A case's citation names the document and has nowhere to put a page or a passage, so this one would be dropped rather than recorded — and a field stated in one place and honored nowhere is how a record and the pages built from it drift apart.", note="citation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.EXTENT_ON_MANY", "A part of a document is a part of ONE document, and this citation would write a leg for several. Writing the same page or passage onto each of them would put claims in the record you never made — you named one part once. Cite the one document you mean this part of, and cite the rest separately.", note="citation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.EXTRACT_NO_SCOPE", "This list of proposed readings names neither an investigation nor a document, so nothing was listed. A list of every proposal in the record would be a scan nobody can act on; name the one you mean.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FACT_FAILED", "The part of your team's Civicsmith that answers that question stopped with an error instead of answering, so there is no answer here, which is not the same as the answer being no. Nothing was written.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FACT_MALFORMED", "A part of your team's Civicsmith tried to offer an answer to a question without naming the question, itself, or how to answer it, so nothing was registered. This is a fault in how your team's Civicsmith was built, not in the record, and nothing in the record changed.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FACT_UNAVAILABLE", "No part of your team's Civicsmith answers that question yet, so there is no answer here, which is not the same as the answer being no. Nothing was written.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FEE_ESTIMATE_WITHOUT_QUOTE", "A fee estimate is a quote: record the amount and the currency as quoted, and the request it answers.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FILES_DROPPED", "This write would remove files the previous revision had, and it does not say it means to. Carry them forward, or name them for deletion on purpose — losing part of a document by omission is not something the record will do quietly.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FILE_DIGEST_MISMATCH", "A fingerprint sent with this write does not match the file it was sent with, so the record would have stored a fingerprint of something it does not hold. Nothing was written. Send the file again with its own fingerprint, or with none and the record will compute it.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FILE_NOT_HELD", "Your team's Civicsmith holds no captured file under that digest, so there is nothing to check or open.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FILING_MARK_REFUSED", "Something you marked about this text (whose voice it is, its audience, its language, the sentences about the team's own doing, or what it names) is not in a form that can be recorded. Nothing was prepared.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FILING_NO_PREPARER", "Nobody is named as the one preparing this draft. Every draft names who prepared it.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FILING_STALE", "Something the draft was prepared from has changed since, as named. Prepare the draft again so it says what the record says now.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FILING_TIER_UNDETERMINED", "The action's risk tier has not been stated, and an unstated tier is never read as the lowest. A member states the tier first.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FILL_UNKNOWN_BLANK", "You filled in a blank the text does not have. Fill only the blanks the text names. Nothing was prepared.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FINDING_IN_SEVERAL_CASES", "This finding is part of more than one published case file. Each case file is its own publication, with its own scope and its own statement of what it covers, so the record will not pick one of them for you. Nothing is wrong with the finding. Choose the case file you mean, and it opens with this finding in it.", note="public-read's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FLAGS_UNDETERMINED", "The flags on another team's work this case rests on could not be read completely, so what must be disclosed is not known. Try again. Nothing was published.", note="case-disclosures' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FLAG_DISCLOSURE_NOT_STANDING", "One of the flags disclosed is not open on work this case rests on: it may have been cleared since. Read the list again. Nothing was published.", note="case-disclosures' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FLAG_NOT_DISCLOSED", "Another team's work this case rests on carries an open flag, and a case may be published with it only if the flag is disclosed. Each one is named. Disclose it, or clear it first. Nothing was published.", note="case-disclosures' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FOLLOWS_NO_ENTRY", "Every stage after the request names the earlier entry it answers or follows, by its position in the correspondence counted from zero. Give the position of an entry already recorded.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FORWARD_PERIOD_INVALID", "The counts are sent for a period from an earlier instant to a later one, and this request named none. Nothing was sent.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FOUND_CAPTURE_MOVED", "This passage was found in a different version of the document from the one a citation of it is pinned to, so the part it names could point at different words. Nothing was written. Search the version the record cites, or cite the document by picking it.", note="citation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.FOUND_MALFORMED", "The passage sent with this citation does not say which document it is in, which version of that document it was found in, or which part of it it is, so there is nothing the record can point at. A document you cannot see is answered the same way. Search again and cite the passage as the search shows it.", note="citation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GOVERNING_LAWS_REWRITTEN", "The laws that govern a request are set by a member with the governing-laws act, and a document created or revised any other way carries them unchanged. This write would have set or changed them without that act, so nothing was written. Use the governing-laws act to state them.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.GROUP_UNDETERMINED", "Your team's Civicsmith has not recorded which team it belongs to, and nothing in this request says, so the record cannot write a document that must name the team that produced it. It records its team once: when it is first installed, or by one act of whoever holds its administrator token in the hosting account. Nothing was written.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.HANDLING_NOT_SHOWN", "What this tool is sent, who receives it and how long it is kept has to be shown to you before it is added, and what you were shown is not its current statement. Look at it again. Nothing was added.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.HANDLING_NOT_STATED", "This tool does not state whether it shares the files it is sent, so your team's Civicsmith will not send it any. Nothing was added.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.HOLD_NO_REASON", "Releasing a scan hold needs your reason, which the record keeps beside the release: up to two thousand characters. Nothing was released.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.HYPOTHESIS_NOT_A_LEG", "A hypothesis is never part of what a finding rests on. Keep it in the inquiry as a hypothesis, and rest the finding on evidence. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.HYPOTHESIS_NOT_INPUT", "A hypothesis is held apart from the facts and is never an input, subject or parameter of a check or detector. Nothing was recorded.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.HYPOTHESIS_NO_REASON", "Say why you are changing or withdrawing this hypothesis. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.HYPOTHESIS_NO_STATEMENT", "Say what you think, in your own words. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.HYPOTHESIS_PROPOSAL_NO_RUN", "A proposal of the system's names the run that made it. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.HYPOTHESIS_WITHDRAWN", "This hypothesis was withdrawn. Hold a new one if you think it again. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.ILLEGAL_STAGE", "The escalation cannot move from its stage to that one. The stages it can move to are listed. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.INBOX_REFUSED", "This was not saved: the list of tasks it carries is not written the way the record writes tasks, so a member could be shown something in it that the record cannot vouch for. The findings beside this say which entries and what is wrong with each. Nothing was changed.", note="tasks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.INTENT_BAD_STAGE", "The measure requires a step the declared flow does not have. Name steps the flow declares. Nothing was written.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.INTENT_NO_REASON", "This act is recorded with a reason in your own words, and none was given. The record keeps why, so the next reader is not left guessing. Nothing was written.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.INTENT_NO_SUCH_PROGRESSION", "The measure names a declared flow the record does not hold. Declare the flow first, or name one that exists. Nothing was written.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.LAW_RELATION_NO_CITATION", "A relation between laws is recorded with the passage that makes it: the amending or referring words, or the court's words, as captured among the standard's own text. None of those was named. Nothing was written.", note="law-relations' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.LAW_RELATION_NO_EDITION", "A standard incorporated by reference is recorded with the edition incorporated, in at most 50 characters, and only an incorporation carries one. None was given, it is too long, or this relation is not an incorporation. Nothing was written.", note="law-relations' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.LAW_RELATION_NO_EFFECTIVE", "An amendment, repeal, renumbering or recodification is recorded with when it took effect: a date, or the recorded event that enacted it. None was given, or it is not in that form. Nothing was written.", note="law-relations' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.LAW_RELATION_SELF", "A relation joins two different standards or portions, and both ends named are the same. Nothing was written.", note="law-relations' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.LAW_RELATION_UNKNOWN", "That is not a relation this record holds between laws. The answer lists the ones it holds. Nothing was written.", note="law-relations' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.LEAD_NOT_A_LEG", "This connection was derived through a declared grouping or a hunch, so it is a lead, never something a finding rests on. Find a source for each step. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.LEG_NOT_REDERIVED", "This derived connection could not be worked out again from its derivation, so a finding cannot rest on it. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.LIFECYCLE_TEXT_UNWRITABLE", "The exemptions or the citation is too long, or holds a quotation mark, a backslash or a line break, which the record cannot store. Shorten it or leave those characters out.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.LIFECYCLE_TOKEN_MALFORMED", "A stage, the entry it follows, an outcome and a due date are each written as one short token of lowercase letters, digits, underscores or hyphens, at most forty characters. One of them was not, so nothing was written.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.LIMIT_INVALID", "A tool's monthly allowance is a whole number of checks, at least one and at most one hundred thousand. Nothing was added.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_ADOPT_CLOCK", "A deadline is put on an action by a member. This request came from no signed-in member, so the proposed deadline was not adopted. Sign in as a member to adopt it.", note="action-clocks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_ADOPT_VERSION", "Only a named member can move a reference to a newer version of a document. The assistant and the record's own machine credentials may say a newer version exists; they never choose which one a finding rests on.", note="reevaluation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_ADVANCE", "Moving an escalation to its next stage is a member's act. The protocol proposes a stage when its trigger is met; a member advances it. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_APPROVE", "Only a named member can approve a filing. A machine may prepare the words; it never approves them.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_ASK_SIGN", "Asking the project's owners to sign is a person's act, and the credential that asked here is an automated one. Nothing was written. Sign in as a member to ask.", note="tasks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_ATTACH", "Attaching an action to an escalation is a member's act. An assistant may prepare the action; it may not attach it. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_AUTHOR", "A standing question is kept only by a member's own act; the machine cannot set one. Nothing was written.", note="answers' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_CHECK", "Asking for a check, taking one and recording one are each a person's act, and the credential that asked here is an automated one. Nothing was written. Sign in as a member to do this.", note="tasks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_CHOOSE_THE_QUESTION", "Setting an assistant to work on a project's objective is a member's act: the objective is the team's, and so is the choice to pursue it. Sign in as a member. No run was opened.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_CORRESPOND", "Recording that an exchange happened is testimony: on this path the entry itself is the evidence, so somebody has to be standing behind it. The credential that asked here is an automated one — it can capture bytes, and it cannot swear that a conversation took place. Sign in to record it.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_DECLARE_ASPIRATION", "What the team holds to is its members' decision, and so is setting one aside. An assistant may propose; it may not declare, depart from or retire an aspiration. Sign in as a member. Nothing was written.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_DECLARE_GOAL", "Declaring a goal, tying a project to it and closing it are members' decisions. An assistant may propose; it may not decide what the team pursues. Sign in as a member. Nothing was written.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_DECLINE", "Choosing not to move an escalation now is a member's act, with the member's reason. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_DECLINE_TO_ESCALATE", "Recording that the team is not pursuing a breach is a member's act, in the member's own words. An assistant may point out a breach; it may not decline it. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_DETERMINE", "Whether a government act complied is a member's judgment. An assistant may prepare the comparison; it may not determine. Sign in as a member. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_END", "Ending an escalation is a member's act, and only once compliance is restored and the consequences are addressed. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_EVALUATE", "Reading what the government answered is a member's judgment. An assistant may summarize the response; it may not evaluate it. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_EXPORT", "Only a named member can hand a counsel packet to counsel.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_FILE", "Only a named member can record that a filing was sent. Your team's Civicsmith sends nothing itself.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_FORWARD", "Forwarding hands an obligation to a named person, and deciding who is better placed to answer it is a judgment about people rather than about records. The credential that asked here is an automated one: it can surface the work and route it as it arrives, and cannot re-address it. Sign in to forward it.", note="tasks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_HYPOTHESISE", "Only a member holds a hypothesis. A signal the machine raised can be taken up by a member as a hunch. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_KEEP_VERSION", "Only a named member can record that a reference stays on the earlier version. That is a judgment about the evidence, and a machine credential holds no judgment the record would stand behind.", note="reevaluation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_MARK_PRESSURE", "Marking a reply as a threat, retaliation, discrediting or legal harassment is a member's judgment, and somebody answers for it. The credential that asked here is an automated one, so it cannot mark one. Sign in to mark it yourself.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_MOVE_ACTION", "Advancing an action is a decision to reach outside this system, or to declare that reaching out is finished, and either way somebody is answerable for it. The credential that asked here is an automated one, so it can prepare the action and cannot move it. Sign in to move it yourself.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_NAME_COUNSEL", "Only a named member can name the team's counsel and assemble a packet for them.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_NOTE", "Only a member keeps a note of their own. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_OPEN", "Opening an escalation is a member's act. An assistant may point out a breach worth pursuing; it may not open one. Sign in as a member. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_OVERRIDE", "Acting on a breach the team has not determined is a member's open decision, made with a reason and answered for. The credential that asked here is an automated one, so it cannot state or change that override. Sign in to state it yourself.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_POST_NOTICE", "Only a member, signed in as themselves, prepares or posts a notice that the team is working on something. A machine, the assistant or an operator token cannot. Nothing was published.", note="network-notices' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_RECORD_REEVALUATION", "Only a named member can record that a finding was looked at again. A re-evaluation is a judgment about whether the finding still stands, and a machine credential holds no judgment the record would stand behind.", note="reevaluation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_RELATE", "Recording how one law bears on another, or how a court treated a decision, is a member's act. An assistant may propose one for members to consider; it may not record one. Nothing was written.", note="law-relations' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_RELEASE_HOLD", "Releasing a scan hold is a judgment two members make and answer for; the machine never can. Nothing was released.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_REOPEN", "Reopening overturns something the team decided to set down, and that judgment belongs to a person who will be named beside it. The credential that asked here is an automated one: it may raise a question and work one, and may not undo the team's own disposition. Sign in to reopen it.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_RESOLVE", "Closing an obligation says the thing the record asked for has been answered, and somebody has to be willing to say that. The credential that asked here is an automated one — it may surface the work and prepare what it needs, and closing work that is nobody's is still closing it. Sign in to resolve it.", note="tasks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_RESUME", "Resuming an escalation is a member's act. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_SET_CONTACT", "Who the team's contact for an action is, is a member's choice. The credential that asked here is an automated one, so it cannot set or change it. Sign in to set it yourself.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_SET_COPIED", "Which other offices are copied on an action is a member's statement, and somebody answers for it. The credential that asked here is an automated one, so it cannot state or change them. Nothing was written. Sign in to state them yourself.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_SET_LAWS", "Which laws govern a request is a statement a member makes and is named beside: the laws follow the agency asked, and somebody has to have read them. The credential that asked here is an automated one, so it can gather what the agency is and cannot state which laws apply. Sign in to set the list yourself.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_SET_OBJECTIVE", "What a project is aiming at is a member's decision. An assistant may point out gaps; it may not set or change the measure. Sign in as a member. Nothing was written.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_SET_PROCEEDING", "Which proceeding an action belongs to is a member's statement, and somebody answers for it. The credential that asked here is an automated one, so it cannot set, change or remove it. Nothing was written. Sign in to state it yourself.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_SET_REMINDER", "A reminder is something a member asks for, for themselves. This request came from no signed-in member, so nothing was set. Sign in as a member to ask for a reminder.", note="action-clocks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_SET_RISK_TIER", "A risk tier tells whoever reads this action whether it is safe to file, needs caution, or must not be filed without a lawyer, and somebody has to be answerable for that judgment. The credential that asked here is an automated one: it can carry forward the tier a member set, and where no member has set one it can leave the tier unstated, but it cannot set, change or remove one. Sign in to state the tier yourself.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_STATE_CLOCK", "A deadline is put on an action by a member. This request came from no signed-in member, so nothing was written. Sign in as a member to state the deadline.", note="action-clocks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_STATE_RECORDS_LAW", "Which law governs a records request is a judgment a member makes and answers for. The credential that asked here is an automated one: it can write the request as a records request that names no law, and it can propose the law for a member to consider, but it cannot state the law, and cannot change or remove one. Sign in to state the law yourself.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_STATE_SEEKS", "Which stages a records request asks the records for is a statement a member makes and answers for. The credential that asked here is an automated one, or no member is named behind it: it can propose the stages for a member to consider, but it cannot state or change what the request seeks. Nothing was written. Sign in to state it yourself.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_SUSPEND", "Suspending an escalation is a member's act, with a reason. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_TRIAGE", "An assistant may turn a finding into an open question, and nothing more. Adopting it, deferring it or dismissing it is a member's decision. Sign in as a member. Nothing was written.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MACHINE_CANNOT_WRITE_ESCALATION", "An escalation's record is written by members' acts only. An automated credential cannot write it. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MANIFEST_UNREADABLE", "This case file is published, but this team's Civicsmith cannot read the list of its contents, so it cannot put the case file together as one download. Nothing was changed. Whoever runs this team's Civicsmith can repair it.", note="public-read's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MEASURE_NO_DENOMINATOR", "A measure of what the office does is shown with what it counted and out of how many. This calculation states no denominator or no population. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MEMBER_ACT_ONLY", "This is a member's act, taken in a member's own name; a machine credential cannot take it. Nothing was changed.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MINTS_BOUND_REACHED", "This investigation has already marked as many passages citable as it was allowed to, so it proposes nothing more and ends. Nothing was proposed.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MINTS_BOUND_WOULD_EXCEED", "This batch would mark more passages citable than the investigation has left of its limit, so the whole batch was refused rather than cut to fit: a trimmed batch would drop proposals the sender believes were filed. Nothing was proposed. Send fewer, or ask the member who opened the investigation.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.MONEY_CHECK_NO_CITATION", "A threshold or share is stated with its citation: a held standard, or your own word for it. Nothing was recorded.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NARRATIVE_NOT_A_LEG", "A shared note is a member's narrative, never something a finding rests on. Rest the finding on evidence. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NEITHER_CAPTURE_NOR_TESTIMONY", "This entry offers neither captured material nor a named person behind it, so there is no way for anyone to check that the exchange happened. An assertion with nothing to check it against is the one thing this ledger will not hold.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NEVER_SENDS_INCOMPLETE", "A tool must state that it is never sent a file's name, a member's identity or an address, and this one does not. Nothing was added.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NONE_EXISTS_READER_DECLARED", "The reader of records requests answered that no such record exists is already registered. It registers once, when your team's Civicsmith starts.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NONE_EXISTS_READER_MALFORMED", "The reader of records requests answered that no such record exists is a function. This registration gives none.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTE_NO_TEXT", "Write the note in your own words. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTE_TOO_LONG", "This note is longer than one note can hold. Split it into shorter notes. Nothing was written, and nothing was cut.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTE_TOO_LONG_FOR_HUNCH", "This note is longer than a hunch can hold. Hold a shorter hunch in your own words, and keep the note as it is. Nothing was written, and nothing was cut.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTE_TURN_NOT_MADE", "Name what you made from this note by the record's own id: the observation or the question your act made. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTE_TURN_UNKNOWN", "A note becomes an observation, a hunch or a question. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTICE_ALREADY_OPEN", "The project already has an open notice, as named. Change that notice with a new revision of it, or stop it, rather than opening a second. Nothing was published.", note="network-notices' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTICE_NOT_OPEN", "That notice is not this project's open notice: it was stopped, or another one is open, or there is none to change or stop. A stopped notice takes no further revision. Nothing was published.", note="network-notices' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTICE_NOT_THE_OWNER", "Only an owner of the project tells the network the team is working on it. Nothing was published.", note="network-notices' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTICE_NO_GROUP_SLUG", "Your team has no name recorded yet, and a notice is never anonymous. Record the team's name first. Nothing was published.", note="network-notices' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTICE_NO_INSTANCE_KEY", "Your team's Civicsmith holds no signing key of its own, so it cannot sign the activity level a notice is always published with. The operator binds one. Nothing was published.", note="network-notices' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTICE_PROJECT_CLOSED", "The project is closed, so it takes no new notice and no change to one. An owner may still stop an open notice, with a note on where the work went. Nothing was published.", note="network-notices' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTICE_SIGNATURE_REFUSED", "The signature is not a valid signature of this notice by one of your own registered signing keys, for the reason named. Nothing was published.", note="network-notices' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTICE_SINCE_BEFORE_PROJECT", "The date the work began is earlier than the project itself, whose first record is dated as named. A notice never claims work from before its project. Nothing was published.", note="network-notices' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTICE_SINCE_EARLIER", "A change may move the date the work began later, never earlier than the notice already says. Nothing was published.", note="network-notices' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTICE_SINCE_IN_FUTURE", "The date the work began is later than today. Nothing was published.", note="network-notices' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTICE_SINCE_MALFORMED", "Give the date the work began as a calendar date, year-month-day. Nothing was published.", note="network-notices' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTICE_STALE", "Your team's Civicsmith holds no prepared notice from you with this fingerprint, or it was prepared more than an hour ago. Prepare it again and sign what it shows. Nothing was published.", note="network-notices' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTICE_UNCHANGED", "This revision says exactly what the notice already says, so there is nothing to publish.", note="network-notices' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTICE_WARNING_NOT_ACKNOWLEDGED", "A notice is public and permanent, and posting it says you have read that. Nothing was published.", note="network-notices' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOTICE_WORDING_MALFORMED", "Say what the team is working on in one line of at most 280 characters. A subject or a body named with it is one line of at most 120 characters, and a hand-off note one line of at most 280, given only when stopping. Nothing was published.", note="network-notices' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_ACCOUNTABILITY", "An act of political accountability states its purpose: asking an elected office to act on the breach, an oversight request, an audit request, testimony, or legislation that restores or enforces an existing requirement. Policy advocacy and candidate support are not among them. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_AN_EXTRACT_RUN", "This investigation was not opened to read documents for what they name, so it cannot propose readings; an investigation exploring a question proposes them only for the step it serves. What an investigation may do is set when it is opened and never widened by its work. Nothing was proposed.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_AN_INQUIRY", "What you named is not a question: it is another kind of item in the record. Name the question itself, or leave it out. Nothing was written.", note="citation's translation, keyed by its code; hypotheses reads it too")
w("refusal.NOT_APPROVED", "A member approves the draft before it is recorded as sent.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_A_BREACH_ACTION", "An escalation's acts are actions recorded for the breach: the action states that it is one and rests on the escalation's determination. Record it so, then attach it. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_A_CONTAINER", "You asked for a whole case file as one download, but that fingerprint belongs to a single document inside a case file. Ask for it without the download-as-one-file option to get that document, or use the fingerprint of the case file's list of contents to get the whole case file. Nothing was changed.", note="public-read's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_A_COURT_STANDARD", "This act is about a court decision or order, and the standard named is not one. Nothing was written.", note="law-relations' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_A_DOCUMENT", "That is not a captured document. A question, a project or an action has no pages or text of its own, so there is nothing in it to read or to point into. Nothing was changed.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_A_READING_RUN", "This investigation was not opened to read inside documents, so it reads none. What an investigation may do is set when it is opened and never widened by its work. Nothing was read.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_HELD", "This file is not under a scan hold, so there is nothing to release.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_IN_EVALUATION", "A response is evaluated at the response-evaluation stage, and this escalation is at another. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_NONCOMPLIANT", "That determination finds no standard breached, so there is nothing to escalate. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_PUBLISHED", "Nothing this team's Civicsmith has published answers to what you asked for. A case that was never published, an edition that does not exist and a name that never existed all get this same answer, so it says nothing about anything unpublished. Nothing was changed.", note="public-read's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_SCANNED", "This file could not be scanned before it opens, so the original was not opened. Its reason is stated beside it. Show the safe view meanwhile, or ask again once the scanner can read it.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_SUSPENDED", "This escalation is not suspended, so there is nothing to resume. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_THE_BREACH", "An act of political accountability names the requirement it seeks enforced, from the standards this escalation pursues, and no other. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_THE_GROUPS_ACT", "These are your own notes, prepared as yourself: they are not the team's act, so they are never approved or recorded as sent by the team.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NOT_YOURS", "A member's own aspiration is declared, revised and retired by that member alone. Nothing was written.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_BUDGET", "A detector run is given a time budget in milliseconds, above zero. Nothing was run.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_BYTES_HELD", "The record holds no captured copy of that document, so there is no text in it to read or to point into. That is a fact about what has been captured, never about what the document says. Nothing was changed.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_CHECK", "A parameter belongs to a named check. Nothing was recorded.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_CONTRACT", "Amount checks are asked of one contract, named by its entity id. Nothing was checked.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_COUNSEL", "Name counsel by a name and an organization, each on one line and not too long; a contact is optional.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_DENOMINATOR", "A detector states the population its count is taken over, its denominator. Nothing was defined.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_DERIVATION", "A detector states how its result is derived, so a reader can follow it. Nothing was defined.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_GOLD_SET", "A false-alarm rate is recorded with the gold set it was measured on. Nothing was recorded.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_LABEL", "A detector is defined with a label that says what it looks for. Nothing was defined.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_LAWS", "The act names at least one law, each by its citation and its level. With none named there is nothing to set: a request whose laws nobody has stated reads as undetermined on its own, and setting an empty list would not make that any truer.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_LESSON", "Retiring an aspiration records what pursuing it taught the team, and nothing was written there. Say what was learned. Nothing was retired.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_MINTS_BOUND", "This investigation was opened with no limit on how many passages it may mark citable, and without a limit it may mark none. The member who opens an investigation sets that limit. Nothing was proposed.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_NOTE", "A dead end is recorded with what was tried and why it went nowhere, and nothing was written. Nothing was recorded.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_OBJECTIVE", "A project states what it is trying to achieve, and this one states nothing. Write its objective and send it again. Nothing was written.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_OUTSIDE_TOOL", "A deeper check needs an outside scanner or sandbox, and your team has none turned on. An administrator can add one in Settings, under Security.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_PAGES_BOUND", "This investigation was opened with no limit on how many pages it may read, and without a limit it may read none. The member who opens an investigation sets that limit. Nothing was read.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_POPULATION", "A detector is defined with the population of money facts it runs over. Nothing was defined.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_PROJECT", "This act or read names a project. Nothing was changed.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_PROPOSALS", "This named no passage or connection to propose. A look that found nothing is recorded in the investigation's log of what was looked at, where it says which kind of absence it was, and not here. Nothing was proposed.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_PROPOSER", "This proposed reading arrived without saying who proposed it, and the record keeps nothing it cannot attribute. Nothing was proposed and no passage was marked citable.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_PUBLISHED_PART", "Nothing this team's Civicsmith has published matches that fingerprint. Something that was never published and something that never existed get this same answer, so it says nothing about anything unpublished. Check that the fingerprint was copied whole. Nothing was changed.", note="public-read's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_PUBLISHED_STORE", "This team's Civicsmith was set up without the storage it keeps its published documents in, so it cannot hand over the published document's contents. The document is published; this is a fact about how this team's Civicsmith was set up, not about the document or this request, and nothing was changed. Whoever runs this team's Civicsmith can connect that storage.", note="public-read's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_RESOLUTION", "An action that has ended says how it ended, and this move does not: complied, denied, escalated, withdrawn, or completed when the team carried it out and no answer was awaited. The record keeps a closed set of endings so that a reader later can tell what actually happened rather than only that something stopped.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_ROLE", "A leg of a question's basis has to say what the material DOES for the answer, and this one does not say. It is never assumed: material that cuts against the case is first-class here, and guessing would put a claim about your reasoning in the record that you did not make.", note="citation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_RUN", "A machine reads and proposes only as part of an investigation a member opened, and this named none. Nothing was done.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SAFE_COPY", "A safe copy is made by an outside tool that rebuilds files, and your team has none turned on. The safe view is still there.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SAFE_VIEW", "Your team's Civicsmith makes safe views of documents, presentations and spreadsheets, and this file is none of them, so it has no safe view.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_STANDARDS", "A determination measures the act against at least one standard the record holds. Name the standards. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUBJECT", "An addressee is suggested for something: an entity in the subject registry, or a record the action rests on. None was named, so there is nothing to suggest an office for. Name the subject and ask again.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_ACTION", "No action answers to that here. An action you may not see is answered exactly as one that does not exist, so this is not a hint either way.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_ASPIRATION", "No aspiration answers to that id here. Nothing was written.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_BUNDLE", "There is no question here by that id that you can see. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code; filings and hypotheses read it too")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_CHECK_REQUEST", "There is no request for a check here that you can act on. Nothing was written.", note="tasks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_CHECK_TARGET", "There is nothing here you can ask a check on: the item is not in the team's record, or it is not one you can see. Nothing was written.", note="tasks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_CLOCK_PROPOSAL", "There is no standing proposed deadline of that name on this action (it was never proposed, or it has already been adopted), so nothing was adopted. Ask for the deadline to be computed again.", note="action-clocks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_COMPARISON", "No comparison answers to that id in this project. One you cannot see is answered exactly as one that does not exist. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_CONTRADICTION_INQUIRY", "No question you can see answers to that id as one taken up from a contradiction, so no comparison starts from it. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_COST", "There is no cost here by that number that you recorded. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_DETECTOR", "No detector (or no version of it) answers to that id. Nothing was changed.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_DETERMINATION", "No determination answers to that id here. One you cannot see is answered exactly as one that does not exist.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_ESCALATION", "No escalation answers to that here. One in a project you may not see is answered exactly as one that does not exist. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_FILING", "There is no draft by that id that you can read here. A draft of an action you may not see answers exactly as one that does not exist.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_GOAL", "No goal answers to that id here. Nothing was written.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_HYPOTHESIS", "There is no hypothesis here by that id that you can see. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_HYPOTHESIS_PROPOSAL", "There is no proposal here by that id that you can see. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_LAW_ITEM", "No law relation, court link or treatment answers to that id here. Nothing was written.", note="law-relations' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_PACKET", "There is no counsel packet by that id and version that you can read here. A packet for an action you may not see answers exactly as one that does not exist.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_PRODUCT", "There is nothing here by that id that you can see. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_PROPOSAL", "No open proposal answers to that key. It may already have been decided; the decision stays readable with its reason. Nothing was written.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_QUESTION", "There is no question by that name that you can see, so this citation cannot be kept with it. A question the team has not asked and one you have not been shown are answered alike. Cite without naming a question, or name one you can open.", note="citation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_REMINDER", "There is no reminder of yours on that deadline that has come due and is waiting for an answer, so nothing was answered.", note="action-clocks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_RESPONSE", "The evaluation names the reply it reads: a received entry of an action attached to this escalation. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_RUN", "No investigation you can see is open under that name, so nothing was done. A member opens an investigation; the assistant may suggest one, and may not start it.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_SHARE", "There is no share of yours standing by that id. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_STANDING_QUESTION", "No standing question of yours answers to that. Nothing was changed.", note="answers' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_STEP", "There is no step here by that id that you can see. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_STEP_PROPOSAL", "There is no proposed step here by that id that you can see. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_TOOL", "Your team has no security tool under that name, or it was removed. Nothing was changed.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SUCH_WAIT", "There is no wait here by that number that you can see. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_SWITCH", "Say whether the detector is on or off for the project (true or false). Nothing was changed.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_THEORY", "State the candidate theory, and any remedy, in words that are not too long.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.NO_VALUE", "A parameter is stated with its value. Nothing was recorded.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.OBJECT_MISSING", "This document is published, but this team's Civicsmith cannot find its contents in its storage, so it cannot hand them over. The document and its fingerprint are unaffected, and nothing was changed. Whoever runs this team's Civicsmith can restore the missing contents.", note="public-read's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.OUTCOME_NOT_IN_VOCABULARY", "An outcome is one of granted, denied, partial, reversed, affirmed, none_exists when the body says no responsive record exists, or none_stated when the body stated none.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.OUTCOME_NOT_ON_RECEIVED", "An outcome, and the exemptions a body cited, are what the body sent back, so they belong on an entry recording something received.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.OUTCOME_UNKNOWN", "Each standard carries the member's outcome: compliant, noncompliant or unclear. One is missing or not one of the three. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PACKET_NO_REASON", "Assembling a counsel packet records why, in your own words, and no reason was given, or it is longer than 2,000 characters. Write one. Nothing was written.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PAGES_BOUND_REACHED", "This investigation has read as many pages as it was allowed to, so it reads no more. The answer says how far it read in this document. Nothing more was read.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PART_MISSING", "This case file is published, but this team's Civicsmith cannot find one of the documents it lists, and it will not hand over a case file with a piece missing. The reply names the missing document; the others can still be asked for one at a time. Nothing was changed. Whoever runs this team's Civicsmith can restore it.", note="public-read's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PENDING_CLOCKS_BAD_BEFORE", "The deadlines are listed up to a date written year-month-day, and the date given was not one. Nothing was read.", note="action-clocks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PERSON_BASIS_NOT_STANDING", "A reason given for naming a person is not one the record holds, or the position it cites was not held on the date of the act. Read the list again. Nothing was written.", note="case-disclosures' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PERSON_BASIS_UNRECORDED", "This case names a person without a recorded reason for naming them. Give each person named a basis: their act or position, a tie, an interest, their consent, an earlier publication, or why a private person is named. Nothing was written.", note="case-disclosures' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PHOTO_MARKS_UNDETERMINED", "A photo this case relies on could not be checked for the people and number plates marked in it, so what the published case would show of it is not known. Try again. Nothing was written.", note="case-disclosures' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PLAN_LINK_REFUSED", "An action started from a plan names the plan by its id and the option by a short token, together. This write named one without the other, or one in another form, so nothing was written.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PLAN_LINK_REWRITTEN", "The plan and option an action was started from are recorded when it is created and never changed or removed afterwards. This write would have set, changed or removed them, so nothing was written.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PREMISE_OVERRIDE_REFUSED", "The reason the team acts without a determination is written in up to 500 characters with no quotation mark, backslash or line break. This reason was not, so nothing was written. The ground it rests on is checked on its own.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PREMISE_OVERRIDE_REWRITTEN", "A premise override is stated once, when the action is first marked a breach, and then kept as it was: it is never edited, removed or added later. This write would have changed it, so nothing was written.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PRESSURE_NOT_RECEIVED", "Pressure is marked on something the team received. The entry named records something sent, or a reply that never came, so nothing was written.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PRESSURE_REFUSED", "A pressure mark says which kind it is (legal, retaliation, discrediting or other) and carries a note of up to 500 characters with no quotation mark, backslash or line break. This one did not, so nothing was written.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PRIVATE_MODE_UNVERIFIABLE", "This tool needs a private mode that cannot be checked before each file is sent, so it is not used. Nothing was added.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROJECT_DOCUMENT_UNREADABLE", "The record could not write the new project's id into its document, because the document sent is not text that begins with a front matter block. Nothing was created.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROJECT_FORK_ID_SUPPLIED", "A fork is given its id by the record; it is not chosen. This request named one, so nothing was forked. Send it again without an id, and the record will answer with the id it gave the fork.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROJECT_ID_IN_BYTES", "A new project's document must not carry an id line: the record writes the project's id into the document itself when it creates it. Remove the id line and send it again. Nothing was created.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROJECT_ID_SUPPLIED", "A new project is given its id by the record; it is not chosen. This request named an id, so nothing was created. Send it again without one, and the record will answer with the id it gave the project.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROJECT_STAGE_COMPUTED", "A project's stage is worked out from its record (the questions it holds, what it has concluded and what it has published), so it is never written by hand. Only closing a project, with its reason, or reopening it is written. Nothing was written.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROJECT_VISIBILITY_NOT_A_CREATION", "Whether a project can be found is chosen when it is created or forked, and this was not a project being created. Nothing was changed. An owner changes an existing project's setting in its settings.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROMOTED_FIELD_UNSTATED", "This is a new item and it does not say where it stands, or when it was made or last changed: neither the document nor the request gives it. The record keeps its history in the order those dates give and decides what may be done with a thing by where it stands, so it will not guess. Nothing was written. Say it in the document, and send it again.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROMOTED_FILE_BYTES_UNSTATED", "A stored file in this change does not say how large it is. The record keeps that size beside the file and checks it against the bytes it holds, and it will not guess one. Nothing was written. Give each stored file its size in bytes, and send it again.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROMOTED_FILE_CONTENT_UNSTATED", "A file in this change holds nothing the record can keep: it carries neither its text nor the address of stored bytes. The record keeps only what it can check, so nothing was written. Give each file its text or the address its bytes are stored under, and send it again.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROMOTED_FILE_PATH_UNSTATED", "A file in this change has no name: it gives no path, or it is not a file at all. The record keeps every file under its name and will not guess one. Nothing was written. Name each file, and send it again.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROMOTED_TYPE_UNSTATED", "This is a new item and nothing says what kind of thing it is: neither the document nor the request names a type. What it is decides which rules protect it, so the record will not guess. Nothing was written. Say in the document what kind of thing it is, and send it again.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROMOTE_SNAP_KEY_UNSTATED", "This change does not say what to call it in the item's history: the request carries no snapshot key. Every change is kept under its own name so it can be found and compared later, and the record will not make one up. Nothing was written. Send it again with a snapshot key.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROPOSAL_ALREADY_ACCEPTED", "You have already taken up this proposal, and the record keeps how you did. Nothing was changed.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROPOSAL_CANNOT_DETERMINE", "A comparison sets out rows and questions for members; it never states whether the act complied. Remove the outcome. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROPOSAL_FORM_UNKNOWN", "Take a proposal up as proposed, take it up edited, or write your own instead. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROPOSAL_NOT_OPEN", "This proposal was already taken up or set aside. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROPOSAL_NOT_TAKEN_UP", "This cites as yours a passage a machine proposed, and you have not taken that proposal up. Take it up first, as proposed, in your own words, or with your own reading instead; then you may cite it as yours. Nothing was changed.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROPOSAL_NO_HOW", "A proposal of the system's says how it was worked out. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROPOSAL_NO_RATE", "A proposal of the system's carries its measured false-alarm rate, a share between 0 and 1. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROPOSAL_NO_REASON", "Say why you are setting this proposal aside. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROVIDER_HELD", "This service is held back until its vendor states how it handles the files it is sent. Nothing was added.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROVIDER_REFUSED", "Your team's Civicsmith does not offer this service, for the reason stated beside it. Nothing was added.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROVIDER_SHARES_SAMPLES", "This tool would share the files it is sent with others, so your team's Civicsmith will not send it any. Nothing was added.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE", "Part of the record this answer depends on cannot be read by your team's Civicsmith yet, so nothing is answered in its place. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PROVIDER_UNKNOWN", "Your team's Civicsmith knows no security service by that name, or the service needs an address that was not given. Nothing was added.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PUBLIC_READ_NOT_REGISTERED", "This team's Civicsmith offers no public read by that name. Nothing was changed.", note="public-read's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PURSUIT_ENDED", "This goal is closed, or this aspiration is retired. It stays readable with everything recorded under it, and it does not reopen. Nothing was written.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PURSUIT_STATE_MOVE_UNDECLARED", "An aspiration is held until it is retired, and a goal is open until it is closed. No other move is accepted, and neither comes back. Nothing was written.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.PURSUIT_UNSTATED", "A goal says what it pursues and what bounds it, and an aspiration says what it holds to. Something here is empty. Write it and send it again. Nothing was written.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.QUOTE_AMOUNT_NOT_A_NUMBER", "The amount is kept exactly as the body wrote it, but it has to read as a number — digits, with an optional decimal part and thousands separators. Otherwise it cannot be set beside another quote.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.QUOTE_ANSWERS_NOT_AN_ORD", "A request is named by its position in the action's correspondence, which is a whole number counted from zero. Give that number to see only the quotes answering that request.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.QUOTE_ANSWERS_NO_SENT", "A quote answers a request, and this one names no earlier sent entry in this ledger. Record the request first, then name its position as the entry this quote answers.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.QUOTE_NOT_ON_RECEIVED", "A quote is what a body sent back, so it belongs on an entry recording something received. Record the reply as received and put the quote on it.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.QUOTE_NO_CURRENCY", "A quote records the currency the body named. The record will not assume one, so say which currency the amount was quoted in.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.QUOTE_READ_UNASKED", "Quotes are listed by the body that quoted them or by the request they answer. Name one of the two — not neither, and not both at once.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.QUOTE_REVISES_NO_QUOTE", "A revision names the earlier quote it changes, and the position given holds no quote. Both the original and the revision stay on the record, so the revision has to point at a real one.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.QUOTE_TEXT_UNWRITABLE", "The currency or the stated basis is too long, or holds a quotation mark, a backslash or a line break, which the record cannot store. Shorten it or leave those characters out.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.READING_PROPOSAL_ABSENT", "No proposed passage or connection you can see goes by that name, so nothing was accepted.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.READING_UNKNOWN", "A reading of a response is one of: complied, partial, denied, or none (nothing came back in time). Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RECOMMENDATION_IS_AN_ACTION", "A determination records what was required, what was done, and why, and never what should be done. Propose an action instead. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RECORDS_LAW_REFUSED", "The law a records request is made under is named by its citation, a short reference such as a code section, and only a records request carries one. This write stated a law that was too long to be a citation, was not text, or sat on a kind of action that is not a records request. Nothing was written.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.REEVALUATION_NOTE_MALFORMED", "A recorded re-evaluation says what was looked at and what was decided. The note is missing, too long, or holds a quotation mark, a backslash or a line break, which the record cannot store.", note="reevaluation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.REEVALUATION_NO_SUCH_CAUSE", "Nothing that finding rests on has moved in the way named, or the finding is not one you can read here, so there is no second look owed to record. Ask for the finding's re-evaluations to see what is owed.", note="reevaluation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RELIED_ON_NOT_PRESENTABLE", "A finding this case relies on rests on material your team's Civicsmith does not hold whole, and everything a case relies on travels with it in full. Find a presentable copy, stop relying on the material, or make the finding supporting. Nothing was written.", note="case-disclosures' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.REMINDER_REFUSED", "A reminder is set on a deadline of the action that has a date, for a day written year-month-day; it changes or removes only a reminder of your own; it is not set twice on one day; and an action holds at most 50 reminders. This request did not meet one of those, so nothing was changed.", note="action-clocks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RESOLUTION_WITHOUT_RESOLVING", "This move says how the action ended while moving it somewhere that is not an ending. Recording an outcome the action has not reached would put a result in the record before there is one.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RESPONSE_FOR_NONE", "A reading of none says nothing came back in time, so it names no reply. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RETENTION_NOT_CONFIRMED", "This vendor keeps some of the files it is sent for its own research. Confirm that you accept that before it is added. Nothing was added.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RETIRED_NOT_CITABLE", "The team has retired this material, recording that it is superseded or no longer stands, so a citation made now would read to everyone after you as live support nobody will look at again. Cite whatever superseded it, or collect the source again as a new item and cite that. A document its publisher withdrew or changed is a different thing and can still be cited.", note="citation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.REVISION_REDATES_CREATION", "This change says the item was made at a different time than the record holds. A change can alter what a document says, but not when it was made: the record orders its history by that date, and letting a later change move it would let anyone backdate something. Nothing was written. Send it again with the date the record holds, or with none.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.REVISION_REGROUPS_BUNDLE", "This change says the item was produced by a different team than the record holds. A change can alter what a document says, but not whose it is: the record keeps who produced each thing so it can be held to account, and letting a later change move that would let anyone re-attribute it. Nothing was written. Send it again with the team the record holds, or with none.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.REVISION_RETYPES_BUNDLE", "This change would turn something the record already holds into a different kind of thing, an item of information into an action, say. A change can alter what a document says, but not what it is, because what it is decides which rules protect it. Nothing was written. To record it as the other kind, create a new one of that kind and link the two.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RISK_PROPOSAL_BASIS_REFUSED", "A proposed risk tier carries its basis: what the proposer read the tier from, in its own words, kept beside the proposal. The basis was missing, longer than 500 characters, or held a quotation mark, backslash or line break, which this record cannot store. Nothing was written, and the action's tier was never going to change.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RISK_TIER_HISTORY_UNSPLICEABLE", "This action's record of earlier risk tiers is not in a shape the act can add to without rewriting it, and the act only ever adds. Nothing was written.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RISK_TIER_REASON_REFUSED", "Changing a risk tier needs a reason, and it is kept beside the change for as long as the record lasts. The reason was missing, longer than 500 characters, or held a quotation mark, backslash or line break, which this record cannot store. Nothing was written.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RISK_TIER_REFUSED", "A risk tier is 1 (file freely), 2 (file with caution) or 3 (do not file without counsel), or it is left unstated, which reads as not assessed. This write stated something else, so nothing was written.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RISK_TIER_REWRITTEN", "After an action is created, its risk tier changes only through the risk-tier act, which records who changed it, when and why, and keeps every earlier tier readable. This write would have changed the tier, or the record of its earlier tiers, some other way, so nothing was written. Use the risk-tier act.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.ROLE_NOT_APPLICABLE", "What material does for an answer is a property of a question's basis, and the thing citing here is a case. A case's citation carries no such part, so this one would be dropped rather than recorded — and a field stated in one place and honored nowhere is how a record and the pages built from it drift apart.", note="citation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.ROWS_INCOMPLETE", "Each standard is compared in rows: what it requires, what was done, and whether the two align, diverge or are open. A standard has no row, or a row is missing a part. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RULE_SERVICES_OFF", "The record's rule services are switched off in your team's Civicsmith until the assistant's measured bar is met. Nothing was read.", note="answers' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RULE_SERVICE_EXISTS", "A rule service of that name is already held; the first one stays. Nothing was changed.", note="answers' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RULE_SERVICE_UNKNOWN", "No rule service of that name is held in your team's Civicsmith. Nothing was read.", note="answers' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.RUN_NOT_RUNNING", "The investigation this names has ended, and an ended investigation reads and proposes nothing more: its work is read against the conditions it ran under, and those stopped when it stopped. Nothing was done.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SAFE_COPY_FAILED", "The safe copy of this file could not be made. The tool's reason is stated beside it. The original is unchanged.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SAFE_COPY_PENDING", "The safe copy of this file is being made. Ask again shortly.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SAFE_COPY_WITHHELD", "The safe copy of this file has not been found clean by the file scanner, so it is not handed out. The safe view is still there.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SAFE_VIEW_FAILED", "The safe view of this file could not be made. The reason is stated beside it. The original is unchanged.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SAFE_VIEW_ONLY", "This file is high risk, so it opens as its safe view. A deeper check that passes opens the original to every member for a day, or you can open it after the warnings.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SAFE_VIEW_PENDING", "The safe view of this file is not made yet. It is made soon after a file is captured; ask again shortly.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SAME_MEMBER", "You already asked to release this hold. A second, different member has to agree before it is released.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SCANNER_UNREACHABLE", "The file scanner your team's Civicsmith uses did not answer, so nothing was scanned and no note was written. It is asked again on its next round.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SCAN_HOLD", "A scanner reported a finding in this file, so its original is held and does not open. The safe view still opens, and the file keeps its place in the record. Two members can release the hold, each with a reason, or a second, different scanner can clear it in a deeper check.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SCAN_PENDING", "This file is being scanned before it opens. Ask again in a moment; the safe view can be read meanwhile.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SCAN_STALE", "This high-risk file was last found clean more than a week ago, and the scanner cannot check it again now, so the original was not opened. Show the safe view, or ask for a deeper check.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SEEKS_REFUSED", "A records request may name the stages it asks the records for: one to twelve different entries, each naming a progression, an entity and a stage in at most 200 characters each, and each stage one its progression declares. Only a records request names them. This write named them otherwise, so nothing was written.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SELF_ATTESTATION_NOT_STANDING", "A document acknowledged as self-attested only is either co-attested already or not one this case rests on, so it needs no acknowledgment. Remove it from the list. Nothing was written.", note="case-disclosures' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SELF_ATTESTED_NO_REASON", "Publishing a document as self-attested only says why. Give the reason. Nothing was written.", note="case-disclosures' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SENT_REFERENCE_MALFORMED", "The venue's reference for this sending is one line of 1 to 100 characters, as the venue gave it. Nothing was recorded.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SEVERED_EDGE", "Somebody already recorded a decision to cut this dependency, which is different from there never having been one. Citing it again would neither reverse that decision nor step around it, so putting the link back is a separate act that records its own reason.", note="citation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SIGNIFICANCE_IS_A_MEMBERS_JUDGMENT", "A determination records whether the act complied, not how much it matters. Significance, severity, priority, urgency, rank and score are members' judgments made with the consequences in front of them. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SIGN_ALREADY_ASKED", "The owners have already been asked to sign this edition, and it is in their queues. Nothing was written. The answer shows who asked and when.", note="tasks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SNAP_KEY_TAKEN", "This write names a history entry this document already has, and it is a different write from the one recorded there. The record never rewrites its history, so nothing was written. Send it again under a new history key.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SOURCE_DECLARED", "This source of proposals is already registered. A source registers once, when your team's Civicsmith starts.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SOURCE_MALFORMED", "A source of proposals names its kind and gives a reader. This registration does not.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STAGE_NOT_OF_DIRECTION", "That stage does not belong to this kind of entry. A request, a fee-waiver request, an appeal or a court filing is something sent; an acknowledgment, a fee estimate, a decision, an extension notice, a production or a denial is something received. A non-response carries no stage.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STAGE_TAKES_NO_ACTION", "Actions are attached at notification, legal tools and political accountability. The escalation's stage now takes none. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_NOT_BINDING", "This standard does not bind this body, so the act cannot be found nonconforming against it. Record it as a benchmark comparison: below, slower than, or above. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_NOT_IN_FORCE", "A standard named was not in force when the act was done, by the period the record states for it. An act is measured against the standards that applied to it. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDARD_SIDE_UNNAMED", "Name which side of the question states what the standard requires, a or b. Your team's Civicsmith never chooses it. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDING_ENDED", "This standing question has ended, and an ended question is never started again. Set a new one if you want it to keep running. Nothing was changed.", note="answers' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDING_NEEDS_END", "A standing question needs an end date after today, so it does not run for ever. Nothing was written.", note="answers' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STANDING_NEEDS_SEARCH", "A standing question keeps one search: a saved search, or a find in a document, a set or a project. Give one of these, not both. Nothing was written.", note="answers' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STATE_MOVE_UNDECLARED", "That is not a move this item can make from where it stands. Each kind of thing has a set of moves its rules allow, and this one is not among them, so nothing was written. Move it by a step the rules allow, or leave it where it stands and record what changed.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_ALIKE_EXISTS", "This work is already an open step on the question. Use that step, or add your question to it. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_BAD_BY_WHEN", "A date for a step is a calendar day, with what sets it: the law, a meeting, or your own choice. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_BAD_COST", "A cost is a fee or a purchase: an exact amount, its currency's three-letter code, and what it paid for. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_BAD_END", "A step ends as done (ended) or set aside, and only once it is planned or under way. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_BAD_FORM", "A proposed step is taken up as proposed, taken up with your own wording, or set aside for a step of your own. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_BAD_OUTCOME", "An outcome is helped, a dead end, or not yet judged, recorded for a question the step is on. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_BAD_PLACE", "A step is taken on one or more questions, in one project, or for the whole team: exactly one of these, and a step is never placed inside another step. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_BAD_PRODUCT", "Name what the step produced by the record's own id: a record, a capture, a passage, a lead or a derived connection with its derivation. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_BAD_REMINDER", "A reminder is set for a calendar day. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_BAD_TEXT", "Write it in your own words, within the length it allows. Nothing was written, and nothing was cut.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_BAD_WAIT", "A step waits on another step, on something arriving, or on a date. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_DECLARED", "A part of your team's Civicsmith tried to register something it had already registered, or that another part already provides, so the second registration was refused and the first still stands. This is a fault in how your team's Civicsmith was built, not in the record, and nothing in the record changed.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_MACHINE_NO_OUTCOME", "The system never judges whether a step helped or was a dead end; a member does. It ends its own step with every outcome not yet judged, or sets it aside with its reason. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_MEMBER_ONLY", "Only a member does this, in their own words and by their own choice. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_MODULE_UNNAMED", "A part of your team's Civicsmith tried to add its own check to every promotion without naming itself, so nothing was registered. This is a fault in how your team's Civicsmith was built, not in the record, and nothing in the record changed.", note="promotion's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_NARROWER_THAN_QUESTION", "This step is a project's own, and a question's use of it would show it beyond that project. Take a step on the question instead. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_NOT_A_LEG", "A step is work done toward an answer, never part of what a finding rests on. Rest the finding on what the step found. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_NOT_ITS_OWN", "The system acts only on the steps it took itself. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_NOT_YOUR_RUN", "The system takes a step only for a run it holds, and this credential holds no such run. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_NO_WORK", "Say what the work is, in your own words, in at most 500 characters. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_PROPOSAL_DECIDED", "This proposed step was already taken up or set aside. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_PROPOSE_NOT_A_MACHINE", "A member takes a step themselves; a proposal is the system's or an assistant's. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_SHARED_NAME_THE_QUESTION", "More than one question uses this step. Name the question whose use of it you are removing. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_UNREADABLE", "This names a step the work serves, and the step could not be read here, so nothing was tied to it. Nothing was proposed.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_WAITING", "This step waits on something not yet met, named here. It starts once each wait is met or removed. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_WAIT_CYCLE", "This wait would close a loop: the steps named would each wait on the other and none could start. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_WAIT_NARROWER", "This step would wait on a step fewer people can see, so some who see it could not see what it waits on. Nothing was written.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STEP_WORKED_KEEPS_RECORD", "Work was done on this step, so its record is kept. Set it aside instead. Nothing was deleted.", note="steps' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.STILL_UNFILLED", "The text still holds a blank the record could not fill, marked UNFILLED. A member writes it in before the text can be approved.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUBJECT_IS_PERSON", "A detector looks at money facts, contracts and patterns over facts, never at a person; this definition names a person. Nothing was defined.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_BOILERPLATE", "A field this reading has to fill in carries filler text rather than an account of anything. A required field filled to get past a check is worse than an empty one, because it reads to the next member as something somebody wrote.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_BRANCHES_NOT_INDEPENDENT", "Two parts of this reading are offered as separate routes to the same answer, and the record can show they trace back to the same original material. Treating them as separate makes the answer look better supported than it is, so a machine may not put it forward that way; a member may still say they are genuinely separate, and that is their call to sign for.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_COMPARISON_INCOMPLETE", "The record holds more material behind this question than could be checked in one pass, so whether this reading is genuinely new, or genuinely made of separate parts, was not settled either way. Not finishing the check is a different fact from passing it, and this record does not let the two read the same.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_EMPTY_LEVEL_UNSTATED", "Reporting that a level of the search is empty means saying WHICH level was searched and where the log of that search can be read. Absence at one level is not absence at the next, and an unattributed empty answer is the one shape nobody can check.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_LEG_UNREACHABLE", "One of the pieces of evidence this reading rests on cannot be reached where it says it is: it is not in the record, it cannot be read from here, or the record has retired it. A reading resting on something retired reads to a later member as live support for the answer.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_NAME_TAKEN", "This question already holds a reading by that name. Names are unique within one question so a member can ask for a reading by name, and a second one wearing the same name would make every later reference ambiguous.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_NOT_AN_INQUIRY", "Only a question carries readings of its evidence, and the thing named here is not a question. There is nothing under it for a suggestion to be a reading of.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_NOT_DIFFERENT", "This reading of the evidence is the same in substance as one this question already holds, so it is not put forward a second time. The reading it matches is named, and adding a duplicate would grow the review pile without adding anything to review.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_NO_DOCUMENT", "This question has no readable file behind it, so there is nothing for a reading of its evidence to be added to. That is a fact about the question rather than about the reading, and nothing was composed.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_NO_RUN", "Every suggestion names the piece of work that produced it, and this one named none that can be read here. What was searched, under which declared conditions, and where it stopped is what lets anyone else check a reading rather than take it on trust.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_NO_TARGET", "That request did not say which question the suggestion is about. A reading of the evidence always belongs to one question, so it asks rather than guessing.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_OUTSIDE_RUN_CONTEXT", "This suggestion is about a question the investigation was not working on. An investigation is read against its own question, or the questions its project draws on, so work on a different question starts an investigation of that question.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_PAIR_DOES_NOT_COMPUTE", "The strength of this reading does not work out over the structure it declares, on one or both of the two things strength is measured on. A reading whose arithmetic cannot be run is a reading nobody can check, and it is not put forward.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_RUN_NOT_RUNNING", "The investigation this suggestion names has ended. A suggestion is read against the conditions of the investigation that produced it, and those stopped being current when it stopped, so going on means starting a new one.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_TOO_MANY_LEGS", "This suggestion rests on more pieces of evidence than one reading may carry. The limit is published in the refusal so a caller can split the reading rather than guess at what would have fitted.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_UNKNOWN_KIND", "A suggestion is one of five kinds and this one names none of them. The kinds are a closed set so that a run reporting an empty search is told apart from a run that reported nothing at all, which no other field can distinguish.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_UNWRITABLE_DOCUMENT", "This question's own file could not be extended in place, so nothing was written. Adding a reading edits the record the reading lives in, and a half-written record is worse than an unchanged one.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUGGEST_UNWRITABLE_STATE", "This suggestion tries to arrive already decided — settled, set aside, hidden, or signed by somebody. A suggestion may only ever arrive as something put forward; deciding what to do with it is a named member's act and no automated caller can reach it.", note="run-productions' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.SUPERSEDES_ANOTHER_ACT", "A determination supersedes only an earlier determination of the same act. The one named is about another act. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TASK_NOT_YOURS", "This task is not yours to act on: it is with another member now, so nothing was done to it. The record says below who holds it. Ask them, or an administrator, if it still needs you.", note="tasks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TEMPLATE_AND_TEXT", "Name a template or write the words, not both.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TEMPLATE_FROM_UNAPPROVED", "A template is drafted from a draft a member has approved. Approve the draft first.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TEMPLATE_KIND_MISMATCH", "The template named is written for another kind of action. Name one written for this kind.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TEMPLATE_NOT_NAMED", "The jurisdiction profile holds no file template for this kind: name a template, or write the words.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TEMPLATE_USE_BRIEF", "The template named is a briefing to counsel: it serves a counsel packet, never a filing.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TEMPLATE_USE_FILE", "The template named is wording the team files in its own name: a counsel packet's briefing takes a brief template.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TENSIONS_UNDETERMINED", "The record could not be read completely for conflicts on this case's findings, so what must be disclosed is not known. Try again. Nothing was published.", note="case-disclosures' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TENSION_NOT_DISCLOSED", "A finding in this case rests on something the record holds in unresolved conflict, and a case may be published with it only if the conflict is disclosed. Each one is named. One in conflict with a record you cannot see is named by its finding, and the published case will highlight it without naming that record. Disclose it, or resolve it first. Nothing was published.", note="case-disclosures' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TEXT_UNWRITABLE", "The text is empty, too long, or not readable as text, so it cannot be prepared or recorded as approved.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEORY_NO_PROPOSER", "Nobody is named as the one proposing this theory. Every proposal names who made it.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEORY_NO_STANDARDS", "A candidate theory names the standards it rests on.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEORY_STANDARD_UNREADABLE", "The standards the theory names cannot be read here, so the proposal is not recorded.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.THEORY_WHY_REFUSED", "Say why the theory is proposed, in at most 1,000 characters.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TIER3_COUNSEL_PACKET", "This action's governing tier is 3: no filing is prepared for it. The team names counsel, and a counsel packet is assembled for counsel's review instead.", note="filings' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TIE_ATTESTATION_MISSING", "Each member who signs a case first attests that they hold no undeclared tie to anyone or anything the case names, including those paid or paying in its money. Attest, or declare the tie first. Nothing was written.", note="case-disclosures' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TOO_MANY_LAWS", "One act states at most twelve governing laws. A request governed at the federal, state and local levels names a handful; a longer list is more likely a list of every law that might apply than of the ones that do. Nothing was written.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TREATMENT_UNKNOWN", "A later decision's treatment of a decision is recorded as reversed, vacated, depublished, overruled or affirmed. This one names none of them. Nothing was written.", note="law-relations' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TRIAGE_ACT_UNKNOWN", "A proposal is adopted into a project's objective, turned into an open question, deferred or dismissed. This act is none of those. Nothing was written.", note="intent's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.TRIGGER_NOT_MET", "That stage's trigger is not met in the record yet; what is missing is named. When it is met the stage is proposed, and a member advances it. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.UNCLEARED_HUNCH", "A finding in this case rests on a hunch. A hunch is temporary declared bias, and it is the one bias that must be cleared before publication: the case must still hold with the hunch removed. Give each leg a grade the record earns, or take the hunch out of the basis, and publish again. Nothing was written.", note="case-disclosures' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.UNCLEAR_NO_QUESTION", "An unclear outcome names what is still open, each question sent back to an inquiry you can see or to a new one. A question is missing or names no inquiry here. Nothing was written.", note="conformance's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.UNKNOWN_CHECK", "That is not one of the checks that reads a parameter; the answer lists them. Nothing was recorded.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.UNKNOWN_EXTENT_FIELD", "Part of what was sent with this citation names a field this act does not carry, so the record cannot tell what part of the document you meant. It is refused rather than ignored: a field that is accepted and quietly dropped leaves you with a citation that looks like the one you made and is not. The fields this act does take are listed beside the refusal.", note="citation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.UNKNOWN_HYPOTHESIS_KIND", "A hypothesis is one of: cause, identity, relation, flow or other. Nothing was written.", note="hypotheses' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.UNKNOWN_PARAMETER", "That check reads no parameter of that name; the answer lists the ones it reads. Nothing was recorded.", note="money-checks' translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.UNREGISTERED_ARTIFACT", "The material named here is not held in this store, so the entry would point at something nobody can open. Capture it first, or record a named person who can speak to the exchange instead — those are the two honest ways to hold one.", note="action-grammar's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.UNSPLICEABLE_ESCALATION", "The escalation's record cannot be extended in place. Nothing was written.", note="escalation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.USE_NOT_ALLOWED", "Only a tool on your organization's own servers may check every file. Any other tool checks a file only when a member asks for a deeper check. Nothing was added.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.VERSION_ADOPT_NO_REASON", "Moving a reference to a newer version of a document needs your reason: say, in your own words and in at most 2,000 characters, why the finding should rest on the newer version. Nothing was written, and the notice stays open.", note="reevaluation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.VERSION_ADOPT_UNWRITABLE", "The reference could not be moved: the question's document no longer holds the leg this notice was about, or the newer version could not be written into it. Nothing was written, and the notice stays open.", note="reevaluation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.VERSION_CHOICE_WHY_MALFORMED", "The reason is too long, or holds a quotation mark, a backslash or a line break, which the record cannot store. Shorten it or leave those characters out.", note="reevaluation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.VERSION_NOTICE_CLOSED", "That notice has already been answered: the reference was either moved to the newer version or kept on the earlier one, and the answer stands as recorded. A yet newer version raises a notice of its own.", note="reevaluation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.VERSION_NOTICE_NOT_FOUND", "There is no notice by that id that you can read here. A notice about a question you may not see answers exactly as one that does not exist.", note="reevaluation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.VERSION_NOTICE_NO_INQUIRY", "There is no question by that id that you can read here. A question you may not see answers exactly as one that does not exist, so nothing about it was checked.", note="reevaluation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.VERSION_NOTICE_NO_SUBJECT", "That request did not say which citation to check. Ask about one question (target=) to check every passage its evidence rests on, or about one passage (content=) — one of the two, not both and not neither.", note="reevaluation's translation, keyed by its code")
w("refusal.WARNING_NOT_CONFIRMED", "Opening a high-risk original needs both confirmations: that you will open it on your own device, not a shared one, and that you will not enable macros or editing. The original was not opened.", note="file-safety's translation, keyed by its code")
